GṚDH, Ⅳ. P. gṛdhya, stride out;
 🞄be greedy, desire vehemently (ac., lc.): 🞄pp. gṛd-dha, greedy;
 eager for (lc.).

gṛdh-nú, a. quick, hasty;
 greedy, eager 🞄(for lc., —˚);
 (u) -tā, f. greed;
 eagerness for (—˚).

gṛdh-yā, f. greed;
 eagerness for (—˚);
 🞄-yin, a. greedy;
 eager for (—˚).

gṛdh-ra, a. id.;
 m. (ī, f.) vulture: -kūṭa, 🞄m. N. of a mountain (vulture-peak);
 -dṛṣṭi, 🞄a. vulture-eyed;
 -pati, -rāja, m. vulture-king, 🞄ep. of Jaṭāyu.
